summary: Test the IPA packages Fedora itself ships
description: |
    No FreeIPA checkout, no build and no COPR repo: the channel images are
    baked with the IPA packages of the guest's own Fedora release
    (FREEIPA_IPA_FROM_DISTRO, see tests/freeipa-env/tf-runner.sh), so the
    compose of the request picks the release under test. The presets to run
    come in FREEIPA_JOBS; `freeipa-env queue run QUEUE --runner testing-farm
    --ipa-from-distro` submits this plan from this repository.
discover:
    how: fmf
    test: "^/tmt/tests/"
prepare:
    how: install
    package: [podman, python3-pyyaml]
execute:
    how: tmt
environment:
    FREEIPA_IPA_FROM_DISTRO: "1"
